{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>According to [their] deeds, etc.</b> Like a man who is zealous over his recompense — the meaning is that He will pay wrath to His adversaries." "<b>[to the islands].</b> To all the islands <b>He will repay recompense.</b> Now His adversaries and enemies are on the dry land, yet He also mentioned the islands of the sea."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 59, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:00:19.192867840Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}